v/tech/dwm/dwm/</guid><description>Overview of DWM Window Manager</description></item><item><title>My Workflow</title><link>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/tech/workflow/workflow/</link><pubDate>Mon, 25 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/tech/workflow/workflow/</guid><description>My developer workflow</description></item><item><title>Why Linux is better than its other competitors</title><link>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/tech/linux_overview/linux_overview/</link><pubDate>Sun, 17 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/tech/linux_overview/linux_overview/</guid><description>Overview of Linux and Debunking the myths</description></item><item><title>Golang and its Philosophy</title><link>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/tech/golang/golang/</link><pubDate>Fri, 08 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/tech/golang/golang/</guid><description>Golang and its Philosophy</description></item><item><title>About</title><link>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/about/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/about/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="about-me"&gt;About Me&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Hi, I&amp;rsquo;m &lt;span style="color: #d79921"&gt;Amiitesh&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I work with Linux and systems programming. I write C/C++, Golang, Zig cause I hate high level abstractions. I work with low-level systems like embedded systems, operating systems, networks, and I like system design. Apart from tech I like reading, writing blogs and music. I write blogs about things that I find interesting and ideas I&amp;rsquo;m experimenting with. I mainly post about tech, music, photography and on the books I read.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Software that I use</title><link>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/my_software/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://embeddingbits.is-a.dev/my_software/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="favourite"&gt;Favourite&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating System:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://voidlinux.org"&gt;Void Linux&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Text/Code Editor:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"&gt;Emacs&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://neovim.io"&gt;Neovim&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Window Manager:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://isaacfreund.com/software/river/"&gt;River&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Terminal and Shell:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://codeberg.org/dnkl/foot"&gt;Foot&lt;/a&gt; combined with &lt;a href="https://fishshell.com/"&gt;fish&lt;/a&gt; shell.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dotfiles:&lt;/strong&gt; I use my own &lt;a href="https://codeberg.org/embeddingbits/nixos-dotfiles"&gt;dotfiles&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="utils"&gt;Utils&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;File Manager:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://yazi-rs.github.io/"&gt;Yazi&lt;/a&gt; as my main and only file manager.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web Browser:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://www.firefox.com/"&gt;Firefox&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PDF Viewer:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://github.com/vedang/pdf-tools"&gt;pdf-tools&lt;/a&gt; in Emacs.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Misc:&lt;/strong&gt; For most of the other stuff like Word, Excel, etc., I use &lt;a href="https://www.onlyoffice.com/"&gt;OnlyOffice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="college"&gt;College&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports and Documents:&lt;/strong&gt; I use &lt;a href="https://typst.app/"&gt;Typst&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Taking Notes:&lt;/strong&gt; I manage my college and personal notes with &lt;a href="https://orgmode.org/"&gt;Org Mode&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="tech-i-like-and-you-can-love"&gt;Tech I like and you can love&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Neovim/Emacs&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Void Linux&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;NixOS&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Org Mode&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Golang&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Typst&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;stm32 and esp32&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>